Qwaszx86 wrote:
> Well I'm not really a newbie, cause I've been playing this game far too
> long to still be this bad at it, but I'm wondering what the recommended
> order is for early characters. Do you head for Sokoban before the
> mines, or mines first?

I head for Sokoban first.  The mines tend to be quite lethal,
especially if you don't have  a light source.   I head for Sokoban in
hopes of getting an amulet of reflection and thereby saving myself from
gnomes with wands of death or winter wolf cubs with breath weapons,
etc.

Any character I lose, it's almost guaranteed to happen in the mines
somewhere.  I recommend not entering them until you have at least a
light source and have achieved a couple of levels.


>I find I often end up burdened (or just dead) if

I personally don't see why you should wind up burdened. There are
plenty of boxes, chests, and bags of various kinds lying around that
can be used as a cache for the less important stuff.  Engrave "E"
underneath the cache and drop a cursed object on top of it and it's
safe from just about anything.


> I try to take the mines first, but sokoban also offers a fair share of
> challenges. Also, by the time you have completed sokoban and the mines,
> where should your character be in terms of level, AC, amount of stuff
> you've managed to ID, etc.

At the *very least* you should be level 9-10, armor class 0.  Can't
speak to the amount of stuff identified.   There are so many dwarfs and
so forth in the mines that you should (unless you're a class that can't
use metal) be fully outfitted with dwarvish mithril, iron helm,  iron
shoes,  a cloak, and either a dwarvish mattock as a  weapon or a
dwarvish roundshield.    Further, you should be able to sift through
the stuff to find a +1 or +2 item.
You should also have a light source from Itzhak's light shop (unless
all he carries is candles).

Oh, and a big, big stack of daggers from the gnomes.  Or a longbow and
a bunch of arrows from disarmed arrow traps.  Or a crossbow and a
collection of crossbow bolts.

And at least one hard gem that can be used to engrave "Elbereth".

The missile weapons are important.  My problem in the bottom of the
mines is running into a Leocrotta or an ogre king or a mumak in the
dark and getting killed in two rounds for my pains.  There are a number
of solutions to this, and the number #1 solution is a light source and
a stack of missile weapons.  

